ull,{"className":"text-xs text-[#4A6080] mt-1","children":[10," min read"]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-gradient-to-br from-[#162540] to-[#0F1F2D] border border-[#1E3A5F] rounded-xl p-5 text-center","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[#2563EB]/20 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3","children":["$","svg",null,{"ref":"$undefined","xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-star w-5 h-5 text-[#2563EB]","children":[["$","path","r04s7s",{"d":"M11.525 2.295a.53.53 0 0 1 .95 0l2.31 4.679a2.123 2.123 0 0 0 1.595 1.16l5.166.756a.53.53 0 0 1 .294.904l-3.736 3.638a2.123 2.123 0 0 0-.611 1.878l.882 5.14a.53.53 0 0 1-.771.56l-4.618-2.428a2.122 2.122 0 0 0-1.973 0L6.396 21.01a.53.53 0 0 1-.77-.56l.881-5.139a2.122 2.122 0 0 0-.611-1.879L2.16 9.795a.53.53 0 0 1 .294-.906l5.165-.755a2.122 2.122 0 0 0 1.597-1.16z"}],"$undefined"]}]}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-bold text-[#F0F2FE] mb-2","children":"Find the Right Tool"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs text-[#839BBE] mb-4","children":"Browse 79+ email marketing software reviews"}],["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 px-4 py-2 bg-[#2563EB] hover:bg-[#1D4ED8] text-white text-xs font-bold rounded-lg transition-colors","children":["Browse Tools ",["$","svg",null,{"ref":"$undefined","xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-right w-3 h-3","children":[["$","path","1ays0h",{"d":"M5 12h14"}],["$","path","xquz4c",{"d":"m12 5 7 7-7 7"}],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}]]}]}]
28:["$","p","15",{"className":"text-[#839BBE] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["<p><strong>GCP</strong> leads in innovation velocity — particularly around generative AI, real-time data processing (BigQuery BI Engine, AlloyDB), and serverless (Cloud Run). Its network backbone is the fastest globally, and its commitment to carbon-free energy by 2026 gives it an ESG edge. Ideal for data-first companies, ML startups, and teams prioritizing developer experience over legacy compatibility.</p>"]}]
29:["$","p","16",{"className":"text-[#839BBE] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["<p><strong>DigitalOcean</strong> shines for simplicity. With intuitive UI, predictable pricing, and excellent documentation, it’s perfect for bootstrapped startups, agencies, and internal tools. Its App Platform and managed databases reduce DevOps friction dramatically — but avoid it if you need advanced security controls, multi-region HA, or complex networking (VPC peering, transit gateways).</p>"]}]
2a:["$","p","17",{"className":"text-[#839BBE] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>"]}]
2b:["$","p","18",{"className":"text-[#839BBE] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["<p><strong>Q: Is DigitalOcean suitable for production e-commerce sites?</strong><br>Yes — if traffic is under ~5K concurrent users and you leverage their managed PostgreSQL, Redis, and CDN. For high-availability, PCI-DSS-compliant storefronts, AWS or Azure remain safer bets.</p>"]}]
2c:["$","p","20",{"className":"text-[#839BBE] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["<p><strong>Q: How has GCP improved its enterprise sales and support in 2026?</strong><br>GCP now offers dedicated Customer Reliability Engineers (CREs) for all Enterprise Support plans and has expanded its partner-led SLA-backed managed services — closing the historical gap with AWS/Azure.</p>"]}]
2d:["$","p","22",{"className":"text-[#839BBE] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["<p><strong>Q: Can I run Windows workloads on DigitalOcean?</strong><br>No — DigitalOcean only supports Linux-based Droplets. For Windows Server or .NET Framework apps, choose Azure (native) or AWS (broadest AMI library).</p>"]}]
2e:["$","p","24",{"className":"text-[#839BBE] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["<h2>The Bottom Line: Match Infrastructure to Intent</h2>"]}]
2f:["$","p","25",{"className":"text-[#839BBE] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["<p>There is no universal “best” cloud — only the best fit for your team’s skills, your application’s architecture, and your business’s strategic goals. In 2026, we recommend startups building AI-native apps begin with GCP, mid-market SMBs choose DigitalOcean for speed and cost control, and enterprises leverage Azure for identity continuity and AWS for mission-critical scalability. Choose deliberately, measure relentlessly, and remember: the smartest providers in 2026 aren’t the biggest, but the ones that align most deeply with how your team builds, secures, and ships.</p>"]}]
